  provenance: "DDG-51 Flight I/II combat loadout, L0 (slice 5). Public figures are
    marked; the rest is AUTHORED (G15).\nSEED 1442, tick 0.02 s (50 Hz, the fixed
    timestep).\nRADAR (SPY-1D) L0: instrumented range 185 km (public: SPY-1 'over
    100 nmi'; the exact figure is not public, AUTHORED). Array height 20 m above
    the waterline (AUTHORED). Revisit 0.5 s (AUTHORED).\nTRACKS L0: drop after 3
    s silent (AUTHORED).\nTEWA L0: evaluates at 10 Hz; a threat is a track closing
    within 3 km (AUTHORED). Bands: SM-2 20-150 km (none loaded), ESSM 1.5-30 km (AUTHORED;
    public ESSM reach is longer, but a sea-skimmer clears the radar horizon at about
    27.6 km).\nVLS (Mk 41) L0: 32 fore and 64 aft cells (public, Flight I/II; positions
    from the Blender layout). 32 ESSM, quad-packed (public: 4 per cell; the count
    is AUTHORED). One launch per second per group (AUTHORED). ESSM flies at Guided
    Fury L2; Pk 0.8 single shot (AUTHORED).\nMk 45 Mod 4: 16-20 rounds/min and 808
    m/s (public, NAVSEA fact file); 600 rounds (AUTHORED); arc \xB1150\xB0 from the
    bow, 1-15 km, Pk per round 0.03 falling to 0.005 (AUTHORED).\nCIWS (Phalanx)
    \xD72, forward and aft (public: Flight I/II carries two): 4,500 rounds/min and
    a 1,550-round drum (public, NAVSEA fact file); 300-2,000 m, 100-round bursts,
    Pk per burst 0.35 falling to 0.08 (AUTHORED). Both are Damage Control's one CIWS
    system at L0.\nMk 38 \xD72 (25 mm), port and starboard: about 180 rounds/min
    (public, M242); beam arcs \xB190\xB0, 100-2,500 m, surface targets only (AUTHORED).\nGUNS
    L1 (slice B1, G35-G41; the L0 numbers above still drive target choice, rate of
    fire and magazines). Drag: the BRL G7 curve (McCoy, ARBRL-TR-02293) times a form
    factor CALIBRATED per projectile; ISA atmosphere; no wind. Sources: NavWeaps
    (navweaps.com) gun pages, read 2026-10-24.\n  Mk 45 5\"/54 (Flight I/II; the
    earlier 'Mod 4' above is the Flight IIA 5\"/62): HE-CVT 31.1 kg (Mk 68/127),
    127 mm, 808 m/s with the Mk 67 cartridge, elevation -15/+65\xB0, train 30\xB0/s,
    elevation 20\xB0/s (public). Form factor 0.9251 CALIBRATED to 23,130 m at 47\xB0
    (public); VALIDATION: greatest range comes at 48.0\xB0 (published 47\xB0). Proximity
    fuze against air: lethal radius 8 m, fuze 0.9 (AUTHORED); 0.3 a hit against surface
    targets (AUTHORED). Dispersion 2 mrad, solution latency 0.05 s, laid within 0.5\xB0
    (AUTHORED).\n  CIWS Mk 149 APDS: penetrator 0.10 kg, 12.75 mm, 1,113 m/s; Block
    1B elevation -25/+85\xB0, train and elevation 115\xB0/s (public). Form factor
    3.2484 CALIBRATED to 5,500 m at 45\xB0 (public). A form factor that far from
    1 says the G7 shape fits this penetrator poorly; no public figure checks the
    curve between muzzle and maximum range. 0.3 a hit against air, 0.05 against surface
    (AUTHORED). Closed-loop spotting: bias 3 mrad, time constant 0.5 s (AUTHORED;
    Phalanx spots its own rounds, public, but no figure is). Dispersion 2 mrad, latency
    0.02 s, laid within 1\xB0 (AUTHORED).\n  Mk 38 25 mm (M242) HEI-T: 0.184 kg,
    25 mm, 1,100 m/s, elevation -20/+55\xB0 (public, Mk 88 mounting). Form factor
    1.2057 CALIBRATED to the 6,800 m maximum range (public; the elevation is not
    given: greatest range over the mount's elevations, at 37.5\xB0). Train and elevation
    60\xB0/s (AUTHORED: not public). 0.2 a hit against air, 0.15 against surface
    (AUTHORED). Dispersion 1.5 mrad, latency 0.1 s, laid within 1\xB0 (AUTHORED).\nDAMAGE
    CONTROL L0: hull 1,000 hit points, 1 per kg of warhead; systems 100-150 hit points
    within 25 m of the hit (AUTHORED: no public damage table).\nSCENARIO DEFAULTS:
    ROE weapons tight; ESSM semi-automatic (TEWA proposes, the TAO confirms), guns
    automatic, CIWS automatic (G14)."
